62e-06,-2.50339189733495e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,23739,315,3108,220,18,14924,702,264,23739,315,3108,220,16,17122,3931,504,1817,9131,13,362,23739,315,3108,220,17,14924,374,1221,21578,304,1817,9131,13,3555,374,279,1372,315,9334,14924,304,279,7329,3082,315,279,12942,6437,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA cube of side 3 inches has a cube of side 1 inch cut from each corner. A cube of side 2 inches is then inserted in each corner. What is the number of square inches in the surface area of the resulting solid?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"73ad80949f0efd118fbf2a7fbf78077d4c5668835efe6b443b70697223d23658"},"seconds":30.913691520690918,"seed":85388474000950438,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we will first calculate the surface area of the original cube and then adjust it for the modifications made by cutting out and inserting smaller cubes.\n\n1. **Calculate the surface area of the original cube:**\n   - A cube has 6 faces, and the surface area of one face of a cube with side length \\( s \\) is \\( s^2 \\).\n   - For a cube with side length 3 inches, the surface area of one face is \\( 3^2 = 9 \\) square inches.\n   - Therefore, the total surface area of the original cube is \\( 6 \\times 9 = 54 \\) square inches.\n\n2. **Effect of cutting out cubes of side 1 inch from each corner:**\n   - Cutting out a cube of side 1 inch from each corner removes a small square from each of the three faces meeting at that corner.\n   - Each small square removed has an area of \\( 1^2 = 1 \\) square inch.\n   - Each corner affects 3 faces, so the total area removed from the surface area of the cube is \\( 8 \\times 3 \\times 1 = 24 \\) square inches (since there are 8 corners, and each corner affects 3 faces).\n\n3. **Effect of inserting cubes of side 2 inches in each corner:**\n   - Inserting a cube of side 2 inches in each corner adds a new square to each of the three faces meeting at that corner.\n   - Each new square added has an area of \\( 2^2 = 4 \\) square inches.\n   - Each corner affects 3 faces, so the total area added to the surface area of the cube is \\( 8 \\times 3 \\times 4 = 96 \\) square inches.\n\n4. **Calculate the new surface area:**\n   - The original surface area of the cube is 54 square inches.\n   - After removing the smaller squares from the corners, the surface area is reduced by 24 square inches.\n   - After adding the larger squares from the corners, the surface area is increased by 96 square inches.\n   - Therefore, the new surface area is \\( 54 - 24 + 96 = 126 \\) square inches.\n\nThe number of square inches in the surface area of the resulting solid is \\(\\boxed{126}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{126}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
